<concept id="bulb13" otherprops="legalnotice_europe-general_egall_2023_20230101_0000912">
    <title>Headlamp (Low/High beam) bulb replacement (Headlamp Type A)</title>
    <shortdesc/>
    <prolog>
        <metadata>
            <keywords>
                <indexterm>headlamp (low/high beam) bulb replacement (headlamp type A)</indexterm>
            </keywords>
        </metadata>
    </prolog>
    <conbody>
        <table outputclass="formatc_none" frame="none" rowsep="0" colsep="0" id="table_k1r_5fj_pjc">
            <tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="0">
                <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
                <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
                <tbody>
                    <row rowsep="0">
                        <entry colname="col1">
                            <fig id="fig_l1r_5fj_pjc">
                                <figgroup>
                                    <image href="images/OJAPE073034.jpg" scale="95"
                                        align="center" placement="break" id="image_m1r_5fj_pjc"/>
                                </figgroup>
                            </fig>
                        </entry>
                        <entry colname="col2"/>
                    </row>
                </tbody>
            </tgroup>
        </table>
        <ol id="ol_n1r_5fj_pjc">
            <li>
                <p>Apply the parking brake and turn the ignition to "OFF".</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Turn off the lights.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Open the hood.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Remove the headlamp bulb cover by turning it counterclockwise.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Disconnect the headlamp bulb socket-connector.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Unsnap the headlamp bulb retaining wire by pressing the end and pushing it
                    upward.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Remove the bulb from the head lamp assembly.</p>
            </li>
            <li>
                <p>Install in reverse order of removal.</p>
            </li>
        </ol>
        <section id="section_o1r_5fj_pjc">
            <title>Headlamp bulb</title>
            <table outputclass="formatc_none" frame="none" rowsep="0" colsep="0"
                id="table_p1r_5fj_pjc">
                <tgroup cols="2" colsep="0" rowsep="0">
                    <colspec colnum="1" colname="col1" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
                    <colspec colnum="2" colname="col2" colwidth="2.343*" colsep="0"/>
                    <tbody>
                        <row rowsep="0">
                            <entry colname="col1">
                                <fig id="fig_q1r_5fj_pjc">
                                    <figgroup>
                                        <image href="images/OJAPE073025.jpg"
                                            scale="95" align="center" placement="break"
                                            id="image_r1r_5fj_pjc"/>
                                    </figgroup>
                                </fig>
                            </entry>
                            <entry colname="col2"/>
                        </row>
                    </tbody>
                </tgroup>
            </table>
            <note type="warning" id="note_s1r_5fj_pjc">
                <p>Halogen bulbs</p>
                <ul id="ul_t1r_5fj_pjc">
                    <li>
                        <p>Halogen bulbs contain pressurized gas that will produce flying pieces of
                            glass if broken.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>Always handle them carefully, and avoid scratches and abrasions. If the
                            bulbs are lit, avoid contact with liquids. Never touch the glass with
                            bare hands. Residual oil may cause the bulb to overheat and burst when
                            lit.</p>
                        <p>A bulb should be operated only when installed in a headlight.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>If a bulb becomes damaged or cracked, replace it immediately and
                            carefully dispose of it.</p>
                    </li>
                    <li>
                        <p>Wear eye protection when changing a bulb. Allow the bulb to cool down
                            before handling it.</p>
                    </li>
                </ul>
            </note>
        </section>
    </conbody>
</concept>
